          "Do not treat unopposed status as electoral security: unopposed results in diverse districts often mask whether support is genuinely distributed across all communities or concentrated in specific segments; deepening constituent relationships with each community — particularly among renters and working-age families — is more important after an unopposed win than before, not less.",
          "Treat the 30.8% college-attainment constituency as a distinct economic and civic bloc: educated professionals in a mid-sized Oklahoma city evaluate on competence, service delivery, and whether government is solving the problems they face; workforce development, educational funding, and economic opportunity are the issues that will determine whether this swing-capable constituency remains engaged."
