          { name: "Dismissing Property-Owner Economic Concerns as 'Privileged'", tag: "avoid", why: "With 90% homeownership and median household income of $92,716, HD-29's property-holding majority has real economic stakes in property tax policy, infrastructure quality, and community stability — concerns that can be dismissed as elitism but are the lived material reality of people who have built financial security through home ownership. A Democratic candidate who addresses these concerns seriously rather than positioning them as obstacles to progressive governance builds durable coalition support; one who dismisses them as 'privilege' concedes the constituency to Republican opposition." }
