          "Build and maintain authentic relationships with Black community institutions, leadership, and constituents — the 32.91% Black population is the foundation of the Democratic 62%, and any incumbent or candidate who assumes this support rather than earning it through specific engagement will find it mobilized elsewhere.",
          "Engage the 9.41% Hispanic/Latino community with the same specificity as the Black community; avoid treating smaller minorities as absorbed into a generic 'Democratic coalition' rather than constituent groups with distinct economic and civic concerns.",
          "Treat the 62% result as a product of active coalition-building, not demographic destiny — property holders evaluating on fiscal competence and Black voters mobilized around economic opportunity are distinct constituencies requiring continuous engagement, and either can shift if a credible alternative candidate emerges."
