          { name: "Partisan Complacency & Ideological Performance", tag: "avoid", why: "The unopposed, 100% result may incentivize rhetoric that plays only to the Democratic base rather than governing for the entire district's actual composition. San Diego's 58.95% white, middle-class, homeowner-heavy core can easily assume partisan loyalty from constituencies for whom economic security is the primary issue — but a representative who campaigns in ideological language disconnected from housing affordability, wage growth, and public safety in neighborhoods with significant Black and Latino populations will find those communities either deprioritized or persuadable by an alternative. The district's diversity and moderate median age suggest a constituency more focused on material governance outcomes than partisan performance." }
