          "Buckson's unopposed victory in 2024 at 100% represents a structural advantage that obscures a significant vulnerability: unopposed races produce zero voter contact, zero campaign mobilization, and zero public articulation of what the representative is actually doing for the district. The next challenger — whenever they emerge — will find a constituency with no recent experience of partisan contrast in this district and a representative whose public presence may be limited to legislative activity rather than constituent service. The racial and ethnic composition of the district, particularly the 22.93% Black population and 7.83% Hispanic population, represents communities with distinct economic concerns around housing equity, educational opportunity, and the material impact of policing and criminal justice systems. A representative who uses the current term to build active constituent relationships, deliver tangible wins on housing affordability and economic security, and demonstrate specific attention to the needs of Black and Latino communities will make the seat durable. One who defaults to partisan rhetoric or assumes the 100% result reflects a safe electoral floor will find those assumptions tested immediately once opposition materializes."
